		<link href="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=68&amp;p=115#p115"/>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Digital Contacts, FM Narrow indication and bug fixes]]></title>

		
		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=68&amp;p=115#p115"><![CDATA[
Today's update..<br><ul><li>Thanks to Alex DL4LEX, the firmware can now access the Digital Contacts in the codeplug. <br>This includes both the Group Call and Private call Contacts<br><br>To access the Digital contacts press # # #, then use the Up or Down arrows to cycle through the contacts and press Green to accept the Contact.<br><br>Although this functionality works fine, I think there will need to be some changes.<br>Currently there is no indication of whether the Contact is a Group or Private call, apart from the name you assign to the Contact in the CPS.<br><br>Since adding the update from Alex, I had some thoughts about the functionality, and thing possibly that it may be better to access this function by pressing Function + # to access the Group Calls (TGs)   and Function +  # # to access the Private Calls <br><br>This would make the functionality similar to # to manually enter a TG and # # to manually enter a Private Call ID number.</li></ul><ul><li>Thanks to Andrew Jorgensen, the display has been improved so that FM Narrow band operation is now displayed as<br><strong class="text-strong">FMN</strong>  and <strong class="text-strong">FM</strong> indicates normal FM 25kHz bandwidth</li></ul><ul><li>I also noticed a bug on FM, where pressing the left and right buttons didn't always seem to cause the squelch to open.<br>The problem was a byproduct of a change I made last week, to stop the backlight constantly displaying in FM when the radio was receiving a signal, but unfortunately my change prevented the audio amplifier from being enabled sometimes. <br>This was actually being caused by the beep function, but it was easier to fix the problem in the squelch control than it was to modify the beep.</li></ul>This version can be downloaded from the usual Tier2Latest location, and in order to keep track on individual updates the link to this specific version is<br><br><a href="https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/OpenGD77/raw/20de400fedca35254862926839726b2e5df73d28/firmware_binaries/daily_builds/OpenGD77_Tier2_latest.sgl" class="postlink">https://github.com/rogerclarkmelbourne/ ... latest.sgl</a><p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Nov 17, 2019 9:03 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
